                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.34479/2609.34479v1/figure/main_figure.png",
                "caption": "Figure 1:Overview of the SentZero training framework. SentZero performs multi-pair contrastive learning between sentence embeddings and weighted-sum patch embeddings (bold red line, lower-right panel). Structured tuples extracted from the findings generate augmented positive pairs through abstract-level mapping. The model is trained with a combination of the contrastive loss (ℒc​o​n\\mathcal{L}_{con}) and the false-negative mitigation loss (ℒf​n\\mathcal{L}_{fn}). Before contrastive learning, the patch embeddings are refined via a residual connection with a text-conditioning module (lower left). At inference, the similarity logits and patch attention scores support multiple zero-shot downstream tasks.",
